{STEP(2, 'Write a simple bio that explains what you do', "Your bio is the short line of text that appears below your name. It should say, in plain English, who you help and what you help them do.", "Example: 'I help coaches and consultants package their knowledge into digital products.'", why="To update: Go to your Profile, tap 'Edit profile', find the 'Bio' field, type your sentence, save.")}
{STEP(3, "Set your posts to 'Public', not just 'Friends'", "When you post on Facebook, you can choose who sees it. For your launch content, you want to choose 'Public.' This means anyone, even people who are not yet your friends on Facebook, can discover and read your posts.", why="Each time you write a post, look for the small audience button (it might say 'Friends' or show a globe icon). Change it to 'Public' before posting.")}
{STEP(4, 'Add a link to your product page in your profile', "Once your product page is live (we will create it in Part 2), you will add the link to your Facebook profile.", why="To add it: Go to your Profile, 'Edit profile', scroll to 'Links' or 'Website', paste your product link, save. Do not worry about this step yet. Come back to it after Part 2.")}
